title: "stdlib.hkdf Tutorial"
author: IVANLI2412
date: 2026-11-23
abstract: HKDF (RFC 5869) key derivation with extract, expand, derive_key, derive_many.

# stdlib.hkdf Tutorial

HKDF (HMAC-based Key Derivation Function) per RFC 5869.

## Functions
- `extract(salt, ikm) -> bytes`: PRK = HMAC-SHA256(salt, IKM)
- `expand(prk, info, length) -> bytes`: Expand PRK to length
- `derive_key(ikm, salt, info, length) -> bytes`: One-shot extract+expand
- `derive_many(ikm, salt, info_list, lengths) -> list[bytes]`: Multiple keys

## RFC 5869 Test Case 1
IKM: 0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b (22 bytes)
Salt: 000102030405060708090a0b0c (13 bytes)
Info: f0f1f2f3f4f5f6f7f8f9 (10 bytes)
L: 42
PRK: 077709362c2e32df0ddc3f0dc47bba6390b6c73bb50f9c3122ec844ad7c2b3e5
OKM: 3cb25f25faacd57a90434f64d0362f2a2d2d0a90cf1a5a4c5db02d56ecc4c5bf34007208d5b887185865
